                and
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ring_learning_with_errors"} RLWE
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braid+group+cryptography+--+references"} Braid group cryptography
          %h2#homomorphic_cryptography Homomorphic cryptography
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} Homomorphic
            cryptography takes a unique approach by allowing the processing of operations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo □
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \square
            on encrypted data without decrypting it first.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo □
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 1
                  %mo □
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  D(E(m_1) \square E(m_2)) = m_1 \square m_2
          %p This field aims to preserve privacy while still enabling meaningful computations on sensitive information.
          %p
            Fully homomorphic cryptography,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homomorphic_encryption"} a subset of homomorphic cryptography
